EXT. SHELLED VINEYARD - DAWN

Rows of broken vines in gray mist. A stone wall half collapsed. A crater at its foot, still smoking.

CORPORAL ELIAS VOSS, 20s, lies in the crater with his rifle across his chest. He listens to his own breath. He has not spoken in hours.

SERGEANT MARISKA DOBOS, 30s, crawls up beside him on elbows, helmet scraped silver. She lowers herself into the crater without a sound.

DOBOS
(whispering)
They're gone.

VOSS
Gone where?

DOBOS
Over the ridge.

He lets out a breath he has held since midnight. His hand, still locked on the rifle, begins to shake. She watches it and says nothing, then lays hers over his until the shaking slows.

A scrape of stone. They both freeze.

A boy rises from behind the wall. A CHILD, 8, in a man's coat, his cheeks smeared with dirt, holding a single bunch of grapes. He looks at the rifles. At them.

He holds out the grapes.

Voss lowers the rifle. Dobos takes a grape. Eats it. Nods once. The child nods back and vanishes behind the wall.
